<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net" agent="gen-ui">
  <diagram id="gen-ui-class-diagram" name="Gen UI — domain model (UML)">
    <mxGraphModel dx="5414" dy="3176" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="2480" pageHeight="1600" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="title" parent="1" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;" value="Gen UI — domain model (UML class diagram)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="36" width="900" x="40" y="-90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-about" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=14;fillColor=#fdfdfd;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;About this diagram&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;One class per Prisma model (backend/prisma/schema.prisma; tables in backend/prisma/init.sql). Foreign keys are drawn as associations, not attributes.&lt;br&gt;Operations are the behaviour the backend implements for each entity; in code they live in the feature&#39;s NestJS service (Alarm.acknowledge → AlarmsService.acknowledge). The usual list / get / create / update / remove are left out.&lt;br&gt;Parameter types such as AuditEntry, SystemEvent, TimeRange and UIMessage are DTOs and are not drawn.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Colours:&lt;/b&gt; purple users and sessions · blue assets and telemetry · red alarms · yellow logbook and audit · green shifts · orange dashboards · teal assistant." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="190" width="390" x="40" y="-40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-base" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=14;fillColor=#fdfdfd;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Entity and TrackedEntity&lt;/b&gt; factor out the columns the tables share (id, created_at, updated_at); Prisma declares them in each model.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alarm&lt;/b&gt; (raisedAt instead of createdAt) and &lt;b&gt;Measurement&lt;/b&gt; (identified by its tag and ts) don&#39;t fit, so they declare their own." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="380" x="1200" y="-40" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="note-legend" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;backgroundOutline=1;size=14;fillColor=#fdfdfd;strokeColor=#999999;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=6;fontSize=11;" value="&lt;b&gt;Notation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;◆ &lt;b&gt;composition&lt;/b&gt;: the part is deleted with its whole (ON DELETE CASCADE).&lt;br&gt;◇ &lt;b&gt;aggregation&lt;/b&gt;: part of a hierarchy; a whole that still has parts cannot be deleted (RESTRICT).&lt;br&gt;— &lt;b&gt;association&lt;/b&gt;: a reference; the multiplicities follow the foreign keys.&lt;br&gt;▷ &lt;b&gt;generalization&lt;/b&gt; (grey, hollow triangle).&lt;br&gt;&lt;u&gt;underlined&lt;/u&gt; operation: class scope (static).&lt;br&gt;[0..1] optional · [*] many · = default value · {…} constraint." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="290" width="280" x="1300" y="600" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="entity" parent="1" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;align=center;verticalAlign=top;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=40;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=0;marginBottom=0;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=12;swimlaneFillColor=#ffffff;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#666666;" value="«abstract»&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;&lt;i&gt;Entity&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/b&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="82" width="280" x="460" y="60" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
